-- title:
--   A-sections through a smooth special point with prescribed value
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring which is a henselian local ring, is not all of $L$, and satisfies: for $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b\neq 0$ there is $n$ with $b\mid a^{n}$. Let $F$ be a field over $L$ which is essentially of finite type and satisfies `IsCurveOver L F` (every nonzero element has a degree-zero divisor given by its orders at all places, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$). Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally finitely presented morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$, and $\varphi$ a ring isomorphism of $F$ with the function field of $X$ carrying each $a\in A$ to its image under `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase`. Let $x\in X$ lie over the closed point of $A$, have no proper specialisations (every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$), and lie in the smooth locus of `toBase`; let $\eta\neq x$ specialise to $x$ and also lie over the closed point. Let $\bar F$ be a field over the residue field of $A$ and $R$ a `RegularProlongation A F Fbar`: a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ with a surjective homomorphism `R.residue` onto $\bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, with $\mathrm{alg}_{L\to F}(c)\in\,$`R.integers` iff $c\in A$, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f\in F$ has some $c\in L$ with $c\cdot f$ in `R.integers` of nonzero residue; assume `R.integers` coincides, as a subring of $F$, with $S_\eta:=$ `SemistableModel.localRing X φ η`, the image under $\varphi^{-1}$ of the stalk of $X$ at $\eta$. Put $S:=$ `SemistableModel.localRing X φ x`, the image under $\varphi^{-1}$ of the stalk at $x$. Assume: $A$ maps into $S$; $Q$ is a place of $\bar F$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring containing the image of the residue field and a principal ideal ring) which is rational, i.e. the residue field of $Q$ is generated by the residue field of $A$; every $f\in S$ lies in `R.integers` with residue in $Q$; an element $f\in S$ is a unit exactly when its residue is nonzero of $Q$-order $0$; $T\in S$ has residue of $Q$-order $1$; and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\chi: S\to A$ restricting to the identity on $A$, with $\chi(T)=c$ and kernel the principal ideal generated by $T-c$.
--
--   This is the Hensel-section step for locality at a smooth point of the special fibre: every value $c$ in the open disc of $A$ is attained by an $A$-valued section of the local ring at $x$, and the section is cut out by the single equation $T=c$ for a parameter $T$ of $Q$-order one. It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_place_evalAt_eq_and_forall_evalAt_eq_zero_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_place_evalAt_eq_and_forall_evalAt_eq_zero_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus) to produce places of $F$ reducing to prescribed points of the smooth locus.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus.lean

